  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   - We start with a parent solution of 47 points that achieved C5=0.3808. Our objective is to find a better solution.\n   - Given the non-convex nature of the problem, we prepare to use a combination of gradient-based and stochastic search.\n   - The key bottleneck is the high dimensionality (47 variables) and the non-smooth objective function (due to the max operation).\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Variables: h[i] \u2208 [0,1] for i=1..n_points, with sum h[i] * dx =1.\n   - Objective: C5 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx, approximated as dx * max_{k} corr(k) where corr is the full correlation.\n   - Constraints: 0<=h[i]<=1, \u03a3 h[i] = n_points/2 (exactly)\n   - We use gradient-based methods where available, fall back to wilders if not.\n   - Sum constraint: We parameterize the sum= n_points/2 by fixing all but the last variable.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - We convert the problem into a reduced optimization with 46 variables.\n   - Start from the parent solution and do a local search with SLSQP.\n   - If the search fails due to infeasibility, convert to an evolutionary approach.\n   - We use a repair mechanism to enforce 0<=h[i]<=1 by clamping and adjusting the sum.\n   - Objective implementation: compute the full correlation and take the max, multiply by dx.\n   - Gradient formulation: If we could have smoothness, but the max makes it non-smooth.\n   - Evaluate on a separate test set for consistency.\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations:\n   - Primary method: SLSQP for constrained optimization.\n   - Fallback: Powell's method for unconstrained minimization, manipulating the vectorization.\n   - Use diverse starting points by randomization to avoid local minima.\n   - n_points can be increased to 94 for denser representation if the initial search fails.\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\n   - Total iterations: up to 20 by default, with time budget of 1300 seconds.\n   - Use the best candidate found so far as the output.\n   - If no valid candidate is found, repair the parent solution.\n   - Check for finite values and integer representation of the seed.\n\n6. Validation and Output:\n   - Final solution must satisfy 0<=h[i]<=1 exactly and \u03a3 h[i] * dx=1.\n   - Compare the best candidate found to the parent.\n   - Shut down early if the time budget is used up.\n   - If we cannot find a better solution within the budget, return the parent.",
